// title: TTP Detection Rule: Suspicious network connection from MSBuild · Defender XDR
// date: 2026-10-21
// product: Defender for Endpoint
// tables: DeviceNetworkEvents
// purpose: Detection opportunity: MSBuild without commands In some detections, we observed the Microsoft Build Engine (msbuild.exe) making outbound network connections to IPs associated with the ArechClient2 remote access tool. In general, it is suspicious for msbuild.exe to execute without a corresponding com
// source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/65d11700e1cb878403d87312acdd6b9a8dd622c1/Defender%20For%20Endpoint/ttp_t1127-001_suspNetworkConnMSBuild.md
// kind: repo
// author: Bert-Jan Pals
// license: BSD-3-Clause (as stated by the repository)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
// Detection opportunity 5: MSBuild without commands
DeviceNetworkEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "msbuild.exe" and (isempty(InitiatingProcessCommandLine) or InitiatingProcessCommandLine =~ "msbuild.exe")
